Claude assumes Lightning restores trainer.current_epoch from ckpt["epoch"]. Your Colab logs disprove this: ckpt["epoch"]=62 but Lightning showed Epoch 34/74. The Manager's fresh-run behavior doesn't faithfully restore the epoch counter — it gets an arbitrary value from the checkpoint's loops state.

Setting epoch_offset=0 as Claude suggests would produce checkpoints numbered 35, 36... instead of 64, 65... — wrong.

The actual numbering bug (epoch 98 instead of 64) happens because epoch_offset=63 + trainer.current_epoch=34 + 1 = 98. The offset is correct but trainer.current_epoch is 34 (from stale loops state) instead of 0.

Real fix: Strip loops from the checkpoint in the resume_weights_only=False path too, so trainer.current_epoch starts at 0 and epoch_offset=last_epoch works correctly.

